# clangd configuration.
#
# The build passes the C23 dialect option explicitly (see the probe in
# CMakeLists.txt), so compile_commands.json carries -std=gnu23 on every
# entry and clangd needs nothing from this file for a file that is in the
# compile database.
#
# The pin stays as a fallback for the cases that are not: a fresh clone that
# has not been configured or built yet (no compile database at all), and a new
# source file that the database does not know about. Without it clangd falls
# back to its own default of gnu17 and reports every nullptr, constexpr and
# bool in the tree as an error. Repeating a flag the compile command already
# carries is harmless.
CompileFlags:
  Add: [-std=gnu23]
